  "id": "Compound::DB00145 - Gene::189",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex, indirect relationship between Glycine and Agxt, mediated through multiple molecular pathways. Glycine binds to Agxt2, which is involved in Glyoxylate Metabolism and Alanine-glyoxylate Transaminase Activity, both of which are critical in amino acid catabolism. This indicates that Glycine may influence Agxt through its role in modulating metabolic processes that are central to amino acid breakdown. Additionally, Glycine's interaction with Gcsh, which is part of a serine family catabolic pathway, further supports a broader metabolic context in which Glycine may exert regulatory effects on Agxt. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Glycine could influence Agxt through metabolic regulation, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
